// The shared bridge model, baked into assets/buildings/bridges.pak by tools/gc_artbake
// (`cargo run -p gc_artbake --release -- --config assets-src/buildings/bridges.ron --out assets/buildings/bridges.pak`).
// One LANE of a bridge (a 1 x 1 tile running along the model's z, the game turns it to its line, rail on the outer +x side only; two lanes make the bridge), with the
// deck's top 0.28 tiles above the water (buildings.rs DECK_TOP). Every faction's bridge shows it until
// it has a model of its own (a model named after the bridge, e.g. "Bone Causeway", takes over).
// Four looks as for buildings: `#1` foundation, `#2` frame, `#3` half planked, then the finished tile.
// Source: the project's design/buildings/source/buildings/ember/timber_bridge.py.
// The timber bridge KIT (docs/29 "Dynamic bridges"): separate pieces a seeded generator lays along a drawn,
// curved bridge, names starting "Bridge " (they dress no building; the test `building_models_dress_buildings`
// allows them). Four atlases of the same Ember timber materials (deck, edge, pier, stone), so each map stays
// sharp at the game's 512 px: deck = "Bridge Deck A/B/C/Broken/Burnt" + "Bridge Stringer"; edge = "Bridge Rail
// Post", "Bridge Rail", "Bridge Rail Rope", "Bridge Lantern Post", "Bridge Abutment"; pier = "Bridge Pier L1|L2
// Short|Mid|Tall" (levels 1-2, timber); stone = "Bridge Pier L3 Short|Mid|Tall" and "Bridge Cutwater Short|Mid|Tall"
// (level 3). Every piece keeps its authored position (keep_origin): 1 tile = 1 unit, origin at z = 0 on the
// water/ground plane the game draws, deck top at 0.28 (DECK_TOP), deck tiles 1 x 1 running along z, rails at
// x = +0.56 (outside the deck edge), piers 1 tile wide and repeated across the deck with their top at z = 0.10
// (the stringers' underside) and a cutwater facing +x. Full conventions: the project's
// design/buildings/source/buildings/ember/bridge_kit/bridge_kit.py. Not drawn yet: the generator comes later.
(
    models: [
        (
            name: "Timber Bridge #1",
